OL,3,CProgramme listings for THU 18 DEC
OL,4,G1930FRadio 3 in Concert
OL,5,     GBach's Christmas Oratorio with
OL,6,     GStephen Layton conducting his
OL,7,     Gmulti-award-winning choir,
OL,8,     GPolyphony and the Britten
OL,9,     GSinfonia at Saffron Hall.
OL,10,G2145FThe Essay: Accompanying Austen
OL,11,     GAntonia Quirke speaks to
OL,12,     Gcomposers who've scored original
OL,13,     Gmusic for Austen adaptations
OL,14,     Gabout their musical choices and
OL,15,     Galso about the music Austen
OL,16,     Gencountered. Today: Ruth Barrett.
OL,17,G2200FNight Tracks
OL,18,     GHannah Peel presents an
OL,19,     Gadventurous, immersive soundtrack
OL,20,     Gfor late-night listening, from
OL,21,     Gclassical to contemporary and
OL,22,     Geverything in between.
